# Every test that writes outputs under %t removes them first (#423).
# `mdir run` and the Python interface keep an output that exists as a
# numbered backup and refuse to write after 99 of them, so a test that writes
# at a fixed %t path without removing it failed after 99 runs of the suite
# in one build tree (Inputs/check_test_outputs.py says how a test is
# checked).
#
# The checker on small cases: outputs next to %t, a directory that
# split-file fills without removing it first, a removal after the run, and
# the forms that pass (a removal first, a glob, a test that runs nothing
# that keeps backups, a substitution that starts with %t).
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_test_outputs.py %S/Inputs/outputs \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CASES
# CASES: late.test: %t
# CASES-NEXT: sibling.test: %t.dcd %t.toml
# CASES-NEXT: split.test: %t %t-mixed
# CASES-NOT: {{.}}
#
# The tests of the suite.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_test_outputs.py %S/.. \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SUITE --allow-empty
# SUITE-NOT: {{.}}
